      "problem": "$\\int 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)+C \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
